sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Drv as Driver (dispatcher)
    participant Sess as InferenceSession
    participant Ring as Context ring (10)
    participant SS as _SessionStream (gRPC)
    participant LB as TritonLoadBalancer
    participant W as Triton worker

    Drv->>Sess: infer_chunk(Request(audio f32@16k, correlation_id,<br/>sentiment_id, morph_config), on_frame,<br/>pass_prev_context, cancel_previous)
    opt no open stream
        Sess->>LB: find_optimal_server(worker_pool)
        LB-->>Sess: worker URL (Redis, free/cached slots)
        Sess->>SS: new stream — new Triton sequence_id
    end
    opt pass_prev_context
        Sess->>Ring: read() → stacked prev_motion/audio_feat
    end
    Sess->>SS: submit_request(cancel_previous?)
    SS->>W: async_stream_infer: sequence_id, sequence_start (first req),<br/>sequence_end (always False here — sequence ends via stream close),<br/>request_id, params: avatar_dir, sentiment, morph_config,<br/>request_id_to_cancel, background (first req only)

    loop streamed partial responses
        W-->>SS: InferResponse(video_frames[N], motion_ctx, audio_ctx)
        SS->>SS: filter stale request_id → hop to event loop
        SS-->>Sess: decode: N frames + per-frame (motion, audio)
        Sess-->>Drv: on_frame(video_i, commit_to_context_i)
        Note over Drv,Ring: commit fires in the pacer AFTER the frame is enqueued<br/>for broadcast — ring tracks paced (not yet delivered) frames
    end
    W-->>SS: empty terminal response
    SS-->>Sess: drain done
    Sess-->>Drv: infer_chunk returns

    opt retriable error (model conflict / no slots)
        Sess->>Sess: close stream (daemon thread) · rotate worker<br/>up to 4 attempts (1 try + 3 retries), pass_prev_context=True
    end
